[
{ type: install
  message: <<EOM
BASound installs its kernel modules in %%KMODDIR%%.

Load the module matching your hardware at boot by adding it to kld_list
in /etc/rc.conf.  The core basound module is pulled in automatically as
a dependency, so listing the driver module is sufficient:

    kld_list="basound_hdsp"

Available driver modules:

    basound_hdsp      RME Hammerfall DSP (PCI)
    basound_dice      DICE FireWire interfaces
    basound_digi00x   Digidesign Digi 002/003 (FireWire)
    basound_line6     Line6 USB audio interfaces
    basound_maudio    M-Audio MIDISport 8x8 (USB MIDI)

A loaded driver can be prevented from probing without unloading it by
setting a tunable in /boot/loader.conf:

    hw.basound_hdsp.enable="0"

The modules were built against the kernel sources in %%SRC_BASE%% for
%%OPSYS%% %%OSREL%%.  Rebuild this port after upgrading the kernel or
the modules may fail to load or panic the system.

WARNING: this software is experimental.  Loading the modules may panic
the kernel.  Use at your own risk.
EOM
}
]
